ible if it relates to:\\nPurely clinical research projects\\nProjects in health economics\\nOther non-lab-based research\\nHowever, it may be eligible if it relates to the translational part of a clinical trial. In this case, it must be both relevant and novel.\\nSpecific criteria for the EHA Advanced Research Grant\\nOur Advanced Research Grant is suitable for researchers who:\\nAre currently carrying out basic or translational lab-based research in hematology\\nReceived a PhD or PharmD less than eight years before the closing date listed above\\nHave at least one first author publication\\nIf you received your PhD or PharmD outside of this timeframe, please check our policy on life events. If this policy applies to you, you can ask us to extend the period of eligibility.\\nTopics-in-Focus Research Grants: If your research focuses on hemoglobinopathies, you will have a competitive advantage in the selection process. Please select the ‘Topics-in-Focus Advanced Research Grant’ on your application form.\\nExtending the reach of our grants: If you are operating in countries less-represented among EHA gra\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"web-ece509e1ea7055ce41222f0b\", \"title\": \"Non-EHA funding opportunities - The European Hematology Association (EHA)Non-EHA funding opportunities - The European Hematology Association (EHA)\", \"source_ranges\": [{\"start\": 4130, \"end\": 4185, \"excerpt_start\": 0, \"excerpt_end\": 55}, {\"start\": 4407, \"end\": 4690, \"excerpt_start\": 56, \"excerpt_end\": 339}, {\"start\": 5152, \"end\": 5172, \"excerpt_start\": 340, \"excerpt_end\": 360}], \"navigation_excerpt\": true, \"text\": \"Left Sidebar\\n1 min read · May 6, 2025\\nMay 6, 2025\\nShare\\nNon-EHA funding opportunities\\nOn this page, we’ll list other interesting funding opportunities for European researchers in hematology.\\nIf you’d like us to add any opportunity to this page, please contact [email protected].\\nCurrent opportunities:\\nDKMS John Hansen Research Grant\\nShare\\nBecome a